Subject: wifi: ath12k: skip links without a vdev when a scan fails

With an MLD AP on a multi-radio wiphy (BE7000 5 GHz split plus MLO) a
link can exist before its vdev is created and bound to a radio, then
arvif->ar is NULL. When the scan request fails, the cleanup loop in
ath12k_mac_op_hw_scan() dereferences it. The cancel path already skips
links that are not created, do the same here.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -5807,7 +5807,7 @@
 		links_map = ahvif->links_map;
 		for_each_set_bit(link_id, &links_map, ATH12K_NUM_MAX_LINKS) {
 			arvif = wiphy_dereference(hw->wiphy, ahvif->link[link_id]);
-			if (!arvif)
+			if (!arvif || !arvif->is_created)
 				continue;
 
 			ar = arvif->ar;
